        "original_id": "3305dac8-14ff-5f0f-9c45-f244cb1f8429",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gotthold Schwarz, Alexandra Röseler, Heike Kumlin, Martin Krumbiegel\n- Organizations: Thomanerchor, Gewandhausorchester\n- Places: Leipzig\n- Works: Bach's cantata \"O heilges Geist- und Wasserbad\", BWV 165\n- Concepts: Bass-baritone\n\nFacts:\n- Gotthold Schwarz is based in Leipzig.\n- Gotthold Schwarz started as a member of the Thomanerchor.\n- Gotthold Schwarz has conducted the Gewandhausorchester.\n- A bass-baritone is a high-lying bass or low-lying classical baritone voice type that shares certain qualities with the true baritone voice.\n- In 2003, Alexandra Röseler recorded Bach's cantata \"O heilges Geist- und Wasserbad\", BWV 165, with Gotthold Schwarz, the Thomanerchor, the Gewandhausorchester, Heike Kumlin, and Martin Krumbiegel.\n- In the 2003 recording of Bach's cantata \"O heilges Geist- und Wasserbad\", BWV 165, Alexandra Röseler sang the alto part.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
